    # Rotomagus (Chapter Three: Hermetic History and Culture, Past and Present Covenants, p28): a covenant of the Tribunal’s past, from its register entry.

    #t173cc131b52b30d7af2c0c ^"Rotomagus" DEF {
        EXTENDS #tMql8hzM4bv6ng0WYA6N9VrH ^"Covenant"
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Years" STRING "875 – 892"
            ^"Register Entry" STRING "Rotomagus (875 – 892): Founded near Rouen by the first generation of apprentices from Sinapis, and destroyed less than a quarter of a century later when the Vikings sacked Rouen. The sole surviving member left House Flambeau in shame, and joined House Ex Miscellanea."
            ^"Register Page" INTEGER 28
            ^"Source" STRING "The Lion and the Lily"
            ^"Page" INTEGER 28
        }
    }

